INV-bikaj's headline -- "61 of 84 AnalysisRun passes produce 0 edges" -- counts
an UNDIFFERENTIATED population. A zero-edge pass is one of three states needing
opposite responses, and a reader of a survey could not tell which:

    A  ran, nothing to find                       correct, uninteresting
    B  ran, could not find what was there         a recall defect
    C  did not really run, prerequisite absent    an ordering defect

Differentiated first, over 405 pass-runs on five repositories: 274 of 322
zero-edge pass-runs analysed ZERO FILES, 26 emitted nodes but no edges (not
silent at all), and only 22 were TRULY SILENT. Those 22 had nowhere to record a
reason, structurally rather than accidentally -- the spec deliberately excludes
non-analyzer passes from limits.skipped_passes, so a silent linker was invisible
by design.

This adds AnalysisRun.silence_reason on the new closed pass-silence-reason axis
(hypergumbo_core.pass_silence, wired into multi_value_field_axis._known_axes),
stamped at the two chokepoints that already stamp nodes_emitted/edges_emitted,
so every analyzer and every linker flows through it.

THE ABSENT VALUE AND `unreported` ARE DIFFERENT, AND THAT IS THE POINT. Absent
means NOT APPLICABLE -- the pass emitted something, there is no silence to
explain. `unreported` means CANNOT DETERMINE -- it read files, produced nothing,
and did not say why. Collapsing them would repeat a defect already paid for once
(a relative --tracker-root read as "not a repo" fell through to a writable
config because those two cases looked alike).

The orchestrator stamps ONLY what it derives with certainty and never infers
no_candidate_construct: only a pass body knows whether it looked for a construct
and failed to find one, and a reason invented on the producer's behalf is a
fabricated disclosure, which is worse than none. So the `unreported` count is
expected to be non-zero and ITS SIZE IS THE SIZE OF THE REMAINING WORK.

SCOPE, STATED RATHER THAN IMPLIED. The Pass.requires graph (INV-hujog) is NOT
built: depends_on CNF and validate_pass_dependencies() have been in catalog.py
since May with zero non-test callers, verified still so at tip, and the sizing
found no state-C population for a graph to catch. The value `prerequisite_absent`
is declared with no producer precisely so a future instance has somewhere to land
instead of being folded into a neighbour; the re-open trigger is written on
INV-hujog. The free-text limits.skipped_passes[].reason is NOT retrofitted: it
has 19 distinct spellings across 29 analyzer files, but across 490 surveys
carrying 39,757 skip records only TWO strings are ever produced, because this
machine has every grammar installed -- the drift is real in a bare user
environment and unobserved in ours, so it is filed rather than claimed as a
measured cost.

Validated on a fresh apollo-server survey (one of the five sizing repos) BEFORE
this commit: 78 pass-runs, ZERO silent-with-empty-reason; 52 no_candidate_files
/ 21 absent / 5 unreported; no_candidate_construct stamped zero times as
pre-registered. The five `unreported` passes and their file counts reproduce
exactly what the old survey predicts through the shipped function.

NOT FIXED HERE, AND IT IS THE LARGER NUMBER: of 185 catalogued pass ids on that
repo, 78 carry an AnalysisRun and 84 a skip record -- 23 (12.4%) carry NEITHER
and are invisible entirely, because four synthesis passes append their run only
inside an `if <output>:` guard. That is WI-tivif's mechanism, corroborated there
with the named instances rather than re-filed.

Tests: 21,991 passed, 100% coverage on all changed files. One pre-existing
exact-keyset test (test_schema.py round-trip) needed silence_reason added to its
fully-populated sample, mirroring the conditional fields already handled there;
re-verified green in isolation (61 passed) rather than by re-running the 680-file
slice for a one-line fixture change.

